ssage="UPSTREAM: mmc: mediatek: perfer to use rise edge latching  in our host design, rise edge latching is more stable than fall edge latching. so that if rise edge has enough margin, no need scan fall edge.  Signed-off-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Ulf Hansson &lt;ulf.hansson@linaro.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit ae9c657e62ac1e565f66e9faed7376a7ff5806e2) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60805 TEST=build chromeos-4.4 for elm and boot TEST=build chromeos-4.4 for kevin and boot  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54090 TEST=build and boot on elm  Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357760 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt;  Change-Id: I7c66669a2dcb3c2fe45b90d99333403e8c8b278d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423914 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="423914" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/14/423914/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I4c3981642fe07ffc01fd2313a7f8d22f187e74a3" commit="d3cca6cba6b2f143e4242774122283d64fa72e04" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Bluetooth: btmrvl_sdio: fix firmware activation failure  In some case, the btmrvl_sdio firmware would fail to active within the polling time. Increase the polling interval to 100 msec to fix the issue.  Signed-off-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by